# Extra page information pattern

Do **not** stack always-visible educational, compliance, or “how this works” cards on app pages by default.

## Required pattern

1. Keep the page focused on primary actions and data.
2. Place secondary / explanatory copy behind an **info icon** next to the page (or section) title.
3. Use the shared component: `@/components/ui/info-hint/info-hint.component` (`InfoHint`).
4. Put the detailed content as `children` of `InfoHint` (optionally a small `*-info-content` component).

## Example

```tsx
import { InfoHint } from "@/components/ui/info-hint/info-hint.component";

<header className="flex flex-col gap-1">
  <div className="flex items-center gap-1.5">
    <h1>Wallet</h1>
    <InfoHint title="About your wallet" label="Wallet information">
      {/* explanatory sections */}
    </InfoHint>
  </div>
  <p className="text-sm text-text-secondary">Short one-line page purpose only.</p>
</header>
```

## Allowed exceptions

- Inline errors, loading, and status banners required for the current action.
- Short one-line helper text under a form field.
- Critical legal consent that must be visible before submit (not general education).
